1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:01,114
Good morning.

2
00:00:01,114 --> 00:00:01,818
World Tours.

3
00:00:01,818 --> 00:00:03,045
My name is Jamie.

4
00:00:03,045 --> 00:00:04,580
How can I help you?

5
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:05,472
Good morning.

6
00:00:05,472 --> 00:00:09,930
I want some information on self-drive tours in the USA.

7
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:11,600
Could you send me a brochure?

8
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,185
Of course.

9
00:00:12,185 --> 00:00:13,940
Could I have your name please?

10
00:00:13,940 --> 00:00:15,600
Andrea Brown.

11
00:00:15,600 --> 00:00:16,592
Thank you.

12
00:00:16,592 --> 00:00:18,080
And your address?

13
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:18,903
24.

14
00:00:18,903 --> 00:00:20,550
Ardleigh Road.

15
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:21,760
Can you spell that?

16
00:00:21,760 --> 00:00:27,040
A-R-D-L-E-l-G-H Road.

17
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,080
Postcode?

18
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:32,120
BH520P

19
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:32,444
Thanks.

20
00:00:32,444 --> 00:00:34,710
And can I have your phone number?

21
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:36,200
Is a mobile alright?

22
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:36,760
Fine.

23
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:44,080
It's 07786643091.

24
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:44,643
Thank you.

25
00:00:44,643 --> 00:00:47,737
And can I ask you where you heard about World Tours?

26
00:00:47,737 --> 00:00:48,581
From a friend?

27
00:00:48,581 --> 00:00:50,550
Or did you see an advert somewhere?

28
00:00:50,550 --> 00:00:53,180
No, I read about you in the newspaper.

29
00:00:53,180 --> 00:00:55,765
OK, I'll get the brochures in the post to you

30
00:00:55,765 --> 00:00:58,350
but can I give you some information over the phone.

31
00:00:58,350 --> 00:01:01,500
What kinds of things do you want to do on your holiday?

32
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:04,713
I'm interested in going to California with my family.

33
00:01:04,713 --> 00:01:08,640
I've got two children and we want to hire a car.

34
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:09,022
OK.

35
00:01:09,022 --> 00:01:14,368
We have a couple of self-drive tours there visiting different places of interest in

36
00:01:14,368 --> 00:01:14,750
California.

37
00:01:14,750 --> 00:01:18,530
The first one begins in Los Angeles and there's plenty of time to visit

38
00:01:18,530 --> 00:01:20,150
some of the theme parks there.

39
00:01:20,150 --> 00:01:24,620
That's something on my children's list so I'd want to include that.

40
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:25,037
Good.

41
00:01:25,037 --> 00:01:27,540
Then you drive to San Francisco.

42
00:01:27,540 --> 00:01:32,248
From San Francisco you can drive to Yosemite Park where you spend a couple

43
00:01:32,248 --> 00:01:32,920
of nights.

44
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:36,400
You can choose to stay in a lodge or on the campsite.

45
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:39,471
I don't like the idea of staying in a tent.

46
00:01:39,471 --> 00:01:40,700
It'd be too hot.

47
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:41,066
Right.

48
00:01:41,066 --> 00:01:43,630
And the tour ends in Las Vegas.

49
00:01:43,630 --> 00:01:44,480
OK.

50
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:47,774
The other trip we can arrange is slightly different.

51
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:49,604
It starts in San Francisco.

52
00:01:49,604 --> 00:01:51,800
Then you drive south to Cambria.

53
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:55,473
Someone told me there's a really nice castle near Cambria.

54
00:01:55,473 --> 00:01:57,310
Will we go near that?

55
00:01:57,310 --> 00:02:00,500
Hearst Castle is on that road so you could stop there.

56
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:00,866
Good.

57
00:02:00,866 --> 00:02:02,694
I'd like to do that.

58
00:02:02,694 --> 00:02:05,620
Does this trip also go into the desert?

59
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:09,235
No, it continues to Santa Monica where most people like to stop

60
00:02:09,235 --> 00:02:10,440
and do some shopping.

61
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:14,370
We have enough of that at home so that doesn't interest us.

62
00:02:14,370 --> 00:02:14,791
OK.

63
00:02:14,791 --> 00:02:18,160
Well you could go straight on to SanDiego.

64
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,350
That's good for beaches isn't it?

65
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:20,927
That's right,

66
00:02:20,927 --> 00:02:24,966
that's a good place to relax and your children might like to visit the

67
00:02:24,966 --> 00:02:26,120
zoo before flying home.

68
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,330
I don't think so.

69
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:32,750
We want some time for sunbathing and swimming.

70
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:37,100
So how many days are the trips and how much do they cost?

71
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:44,449
The first one I told you about is a self-drive tour through California which lasts twelve days

72
00:02:44,449 --> 00:02:46,610
and covers 2,020 kilometres.

73
00:02:46,610 --> 00:02:53,877
The shortest journey is 206 km and the longest is 632 kilometres.

74
00:02:53,877 --> 00:02:57,510
The cost is 525 per person.

75
00:02:57,510 --> 00:03:02,180
That includes accommodation, car rental and a flight but no meals.

76
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:02,648
OK.

77
00:03:02,648 --> 00:03:04,520
And the other trip?

78
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:09,481
That lasts nine days but you spend only three days on the road.

79
00:03:09,481 --> 00:03:11,770
You cover about 980 kilometres altogether.

80
00:03:11,770 --> 00:03:13,550
So is that cheaper then?

81
00:03:13,550 --> 00:03:16,114
Yes, it's almost a hundred pounds cheaper.

82
00:03:16,114 --> 00:03:17,579
It's 429 per person,

83
00:03:17,579 --> 00:03:19,410
which is a good deal.

84
00:03:19,410 --> 00:03:23,120
So that covers accommodation and car hire.

85
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,710
What about flights?

86
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:25,765
They aren't included.

87
00:03:25,765 --> 00:03:28,580
But these hotels offer dinner in the price.

88
00:03:28,580 --> 00:03:28,873
OK.

89
00:03:28,873 --> 00:03:30,341
Well, thank you very much.

90
00:03:30,341 --> 00:03:34,450
I'll be in touch when I've had a chance to look at the brochure.

91
00:03:34,450 --> 00:03:35,954
I'm pleased to help.

92
00:03:35,954 --> 00:03:36,330
Goodbye.

93
00:03:36,330 --> 00:03:37,000
Goodbye.
